%% YieldGuard — LLD 3/5: Runtime sequence, PRE-RUN batch risk path (FR-8)
%% This is the half of the S1 brief -- flag upcoming batches BEFORE they run --
%% that had no diagram at all in the original LLD set. The PRD calls it the
%% differentiator worth protecting over polish, so it needs to be visible to a judge.
%% Note what is absent here: no wafer map, no test results. They do not exist yet.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Mgr as Fab Ops Manager
    participant Bob as IBM Bob (agent loop)
    participant MCP as YieldGuard MCP Server
    participant Sim as Similarity Model (Track 2)
    participant VDB as Vector Store
    participant Tel as Simulated SECS/GEM
    participant WX as watsonx.ai (Granite)

    Mgr->>Bob: Which of tomorrow's 12 lots should I worry about?
    Note over Bob: No wafer maps and no test data exist for these lots.<br/>classify_wafer_map and score_sensor_anomaly are<br/>UNAVAILABLE by construction — only planned params exist.

    loop for each planned lot
        Bob->>MCP: flag_at_risk_batch(lot_id, planned_process_params)
        MCP->>Sim: cosine(planned_params, low-yield centroid)
        Sim-->>MCP: similarity
        MCP->>VDB: nearest historical low-yield profiles
        VDB-->>MCP: matched_case_ids
        MCP-->>Bob: at_risk:true, similarity_to_historical_low_yield:0.74,<br/>matched_case_ids:[HC-018,HC-042]
    end

    Note over Bob: Bob triages: only lots over threshold get<br/>the expensive explain-why follow-up

    alt at least one lot flagged at_risk
        Bob->>MCP: retrieve_similar_cases(defect_class_of_matched_cases,<br/>planned_params_as_signature)
        MCP->>VDB: similarity search
        VDB-->>MCP: precedent cases + their confirmed root causes
        MCP-->>Bob: cases[]

        Bob->>MCP: query_telemetry(planned_equipment_ids, 14d)
        Note right of MCP: Is the tool these lots are ABOUT to run on<br/>already drifting? This is the leading indicator.
        MCP->>Tel: current tool state for the planned chamber
        Tel-->>MCP: trend series
        MCP-->>Bob: telemetry[]

        Bob->>MCP: rank_root_causes(classification=null, anomaly=null,<br/>cases, telemetry)
        Note over MCP,WX: Degraded evidence bundle — two of four inputs are null.<br/>Prompt must yield PRE-RUN risk drivers, not a post-mortem<br/>diagnosis of a failure that has not happened.
        MCP->>WX: reasoning call, pre-run mode
        WX-->>MCP: ranked risk drivers + evidence
        MCP-->>Bob: hypotheses:[description:planned slurry flow 0.79<br/>resembles HC-018 pre-excursion profile, confidence:0.64,<br/>evidence_summary:matched HC-018 (sim 0.74) · CMP-03<br/>slurry_flow_rate already -1.8 sigma]

        Bob->>MCP: get_corrective_action_playbook(top_hypothesis)
        MCP->>WX: pre-run preventive actions
        WX-->>MCP: actions
        MCP-->>Bob: actions:[description:Re-qualify CMP-03 slurry<br/>delivery before releasing L-4502/L-4507, priority:high]

        Bob-->>Mgr: 2 of 12 lots flagged, with why and what to do first
        Note over Mgr: Framed as a TRIAGE SIGNAL for engineer review,<br/>not an automated go/no-go gate (PRD Section 15).
    else no lot over threshold
        Bob-->>Mgr: No lot resembles a historical low-yield profile above<br/>threshold. Reporting the threshold used, not just all clear.
    end

    opt Outcome known later — closes the prediction loop
        Mgr->>Bob: L-4502 ran fine actually.
        Bob->>MCP: submit_feedback(hypothesis_id, rejected, ran at 94%)
        MCP->>VDB: write rejection — prevents this false positive<br/>from being reinforced as precedent
        MCP-->>Bob: status:ok
    end
